INT. LIGHTHOUSE KEEPER'S KITCHEN - NIGHT

A round room wrapped around a spiral stair. A kettle sits on a coal stove. A wall phone with a cord like a pigtail hangs by the door. Rain hammers the little windows.

PERPETUA "PEPPER" ADEYEMI-HALL (50s, oilskin coat, tired humor) is wrestling a very large frozen turkey into a very small oven.

PEPPER
In you go. Nobody's judging.

The turkey does not go in. She tries it sideways.

PEPPER (CONT'D)
Wide-body. Fine. Everybody's built different.

DESMOND "DEZ" CARVALHO (30s, a nervous inspector in a suit that has never seen weather) stands dripping on the mat, holding a clipboard like a shield.

DEZ
Ms. Adeyemi-Hall, I'm required to note that the lamp is, technically, off.

PEPPER
The lamp is resting.

DEZ
Ships rely on that lamp.

PEPPER
Ships rely on a lot of things. They also rely on a roast.

DEZ
There is a ship out there right now.

PEPPER
There's always a ship out there. Sit. Sit! You're making the room look nervous.

Dez sits on a stool. It wobbles. He grips the table.

DEZ
I was told the Board of Maritime Safety had been in touch.

PEPPER
The Board of Maritime Safety sent me a calendar. January's a puffin.

She finally jams the turkey in and slams the oven door. Victory. She dusts her hands. Dez writes something down.

PEPPER (CONT'D)
What did you just write?

DEZ
"Turkey."

PEPPER
Good. Underline it.

The wall phone RINGS. Both of them look at it. It RINGS again. Pepper does not move.

DEZ
Aren't you going to...?

PEPPER
It's the same man every Thursday. He wants to know about the weather.

DEZ
It's Thursday?

PEPPER
It's always Thursday somewhere. Answer it, if you're so keen.

Dez picks up the receiver. Holds it at arm's length.

X

Dez goes white. He holds the receiver out to Pepper. She doesn't take it.

DEZ
(whisper)
A ferry. There's a ferry.

PEPPER
Tell him the lamp is resting.

DEZ
I will not tell him the lamp is resting!

BRANNIGAN (V.O.)
(over phone)
Hello? Is someone there? Is that the keeper?

Dez clamps the phone to his chest, panting. Pepper sighs, as if he's asked her to move a sofa. She heaves herself up, sets the kettle aside, and takes the receiver.

PEPPER
(into phone)
Marguerite. Pepper. I'll have her lit in four minutes. Stand off to starboard and sing something.

BRANNIGAN (V.O.)
(over phone)
Four minutes? It's a thirty-minute climb.

PEPPER
(into phone)
Not if you know the stairs.

She hangs up. Walks to the spiral stair. Dez follows, clipboard abandoned.

DEZ
You can't climb it in four minutes.

PEPPER
No.

She opens a panel beside the stair. Inside: a small brass lever and a rope. She hauls the lever. Far above, something grinds, then flares. A white sweep of light crosses the window and the kitchen goes bright, then dark, then bright.

Dez stares.

DEZ
It was always automatic?

PEPPER
Since nineteen-eighty. I just like to see who turns up.

DEZ
Then why was it off?

PEPPER
I switched it off at six. To see who'd notice.

She picks up the kettle again. Dez opens his mouth, closes it, and picks up his clipboard.

The kitchen door BANGS open. A wet, enormous man in a ferry captain's cap fills the frame: CAPTAIN OLUWASEUN BRANNIGAN (60s, a tide-beaten face, furious), a handheld radio still crackling at his belt. Behind him, the storm.

BRANNIGAN
Which of you turned my lighthouse off?

Pepper points at Dez without looking.

DEZ
Me?!

BRANNIGAN
(to Dez, advancing)
You? You're the one?

DEZ
No! I'm the inspector!

BRANNIGAN
Inspector of what?

PEPPER
Turkey.

Brannigan stops. Smells the air. Sniffs again. His face softens by degrees.

BRANNIGAN
Is that sage?

PEPPER
Take your coat off, Seun. The phone can have your voice. There's enough for everyone.

BRANNIGAN
(still suspicious)
How much enough?

PEPPER
Wide-body enough.

Brannigan peels off his dripping coat. Dez, bewildered, makes room on the stool. It wobbles. All three men and the turkey settle in as the lighthouse beam wheels slowly past the window, over and over.

DEZ
(quietly, to himself)
Underline "turkey."

He does.
